The minimax() function accepts five parameters:

* depth: The current depth of the tree.
* node_index: The index of the current node.
* is_max: Indicates whether the current player is the Maximizer.
* scores: The list containing the leaf-node scores.
* height: The total height of the game tree.

When the current depth reaches the tree height, the function returns the corresponding leaf score.

If is_max is True, the function evaluates the two child nodes and returns the maximum value.

If is_max is False, the function evaluates the two child nodes and returns the minimum value.

The function calls itself recursively until the complete game tree has been evaluated. Finally, the optimal value is printed.

